From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] server, kernelbase, ntdll: machine keys without a descriptor, registry virtualization (3764)

server, kernelbase, ntdll: machine keys without a descriptor, registry virtualization

SHIPPED HOLE: keys loaded from system.reg carry no security descriptor
(descriptors are not saved), and check_object_access() lets everyone do
everything with an object that has none. In a shared prefix any user could
write HKLM\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Run (an autostart for
every user), Windows NT\CurrentVersion, Session Manager, ...; only
HKLM\Software\Policies and keys made after the server started were
protected. Found while writing 3756 (a restricted token "could write HKLM").

server: in a system prefix a key under \Registry\Machine without a
descriptor is checked against the one Windows gives machine keys: SYSTEM and
Administrators full control, Users, Authenticated Users and sandboxes read,
CREATOR OWNER full control below. GetSecurityInfo shows it. Not covered:
the display configuration keys (they now also include the three
DeviceClasses interface keys found by tracing a standard user's session),
keys with a descriptor, HKCU and other hives. SG_TRACE_MKEY_DENY=1 makes the
server log each denial by the default.

ntdll: RtlGetVersion opened HKLM\...\CurrentVersion, Control\Windows and
Control\ProductOptions with KEY_ALL_ACCESS to read them; now KEY_QUERY_VALUE.

kernelbase: registry virtualization, as Windows does it for old programs
(UAC): for a 32-bit process whose manifest has no requestedExecutionLevel,
run by a user who is not an administrator and not elevated, a denied write
under HKLM\Software goes to HKCU\Software\Classes\VirtualStore\MACHINE\
SOFTWARE (Wow6432Node for a 32-bit program), and reading sees the store over
the machine's key. Not for 64-bit or manifested programs, nor for HKLM\
Software\Classes, Microsoft\Windows, Microsoft\Windows NT. Uses the merged
view of HKEY_CLASSES_ROOT.
CORE review: security. SHIPPED HOLE: candidate for an early release.
---
